From 0fec656d08aa59ad3ea1bba148a4f7e5618fd4d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luiz Augusto von Dentz <luiz.von.dentz@intel.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: btusb: Invert LE State flag to set invalid rather then valid

Bluetooth: btusb: Invert LE State flag to set invalid rather then valid

This inverts the LE State flag so by default we assume the controllers
would report valid states rather than invalid so it is inline with the
respective quirk (HCI_QUIRK_BROKEN_LE_STATES).

Signed-off-by: Luiz Augusto von Dentz <luiz.von.dentz@intel.com>

Upstream-Status: Backport [https://github.com/torvalds/linux/commit/0fec656d08aa59ad3ea1bba148a4f7e5618fd4d3]

[Adapt the device table context to NVIDIA 6.8.12. Remove the old opt-in
flags and retain the upstream opt-out semantics. The HCI core supported-
state checks remain unchanged. Controlled Thor test004912 proves the
blanket quirk blocked initiation with two live peripheral links.]

